    description: "framework_patterns.py PatternSpec supports symbol_name/symbol_kind/symbol_path/modifiers_exclude but has NO is_test_file field, so the matcher cannot honor Symbol.supply_chain.is_test_file (which IS correctly set). Consequently naming-conventions concepts fire on test code: `service_by_name` on 4 test-fixture `MyService` classes and `controller_by_name` on a pytest class `TestMultipleActionsSameController`, all is_test_file=true. The naming-conventions.yaml comment claims test exclusion the regex doesn't deliver. Fix: add an is_test_file field to PatternSpec/the matcher engine and gate naming-conventions concepts off test files. (Distinct from WI-mozum, which is the supply_chain TEST_FILE_PATTERNS layer.) Surfaced via dogfooding; blinded severity 3/5."  # 89ad
    fields: {}  # 89ad
